From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: the clipboard of remote desktop sessions

Remote desktop apps (RustDesk, AnyDesk, Deskflow) share the clipboard with
the other computer through xdg-desktop-portal's Clipboard portal, part of
their RemoteDesktop session (0023). The NickelOS backend
(xdg-desktop-portal-nickel) reaches ChromeOS's clipboard through
VmApplicationsService, with the session's control token: only while the
user lets the app control the device, so no other process reads the
clipboard through here.

- NickelClipboardFormats(token) -> (state, MIME types): the clipboard's
  sequence token (new with every change; the backend watches it once a
  second) and what it holds: text (text/plain;charset=utf-8, text/plain,
  UTF8_STRING, STRING, TEXT), text/html, image/png.
- NickelClipboardRead(token, MIME type) -> (found, data): text or HTML in
  UTF-8, or the PNG.
- NickelClipboardWrite(token, MIME type, data) -> (done): text or HTML.
  Pictures are not taken: decoding another computer's images in Chrome's
  browser process is not worth the risk.
- NickelRemoteDesktop::IsActive(token).

